      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.63,
      "end_seconds": 291.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "You can relax now. Let me tell you where I've got to. This looks most like possible white-coat blood pressure. I'd also keep early hypertension in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.37,
      "end_seconds": 294.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.17,
      "end_seconds": 329.58,
      "duration_seconds": 34.41,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible white-coat blood pressure do well once it's treated properly. I'm going to order a 24-hour blood pressure monitor, for raised clinic blood pressure. Cut back on salt and do a week of home readings. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'll want another look after the monitor. Okay, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
